It has been possible for a long time to select a text font for a math alp=
habet in unicode-math, but this feature was probably not documented very =
well.
If you try to select a particular unicode range such as \mathbfup and a f=
ont simply doesn=92t have it (well, it only checks =93A=94 I think), the =
remapping doesn=92t occur and you get the ascii-range glyphs:

