\usepackage{fontspec}
\usepackage{unicode-math}
\setmainfont{texgyretermes-regular.otf}
\setmathfont[range=3D\mathbfup]{texgyreheros-bold.otf}
\begin{document}
text \textbf{bold}
\[ m+a+t+h \quad \mathbf{b+o+l+d} \]
\end{document}

BUT this doesn=92t work properly with \mathit, because unicode-math hasn=92=
t distinguished =93math alphabetic symbols=94 from =93math text font=94.

